# FoodUs relay — Caddy front door (TEMPLATE).
#
# Public mechanism, private values: `relay.example.com` below is a placeholder. Copy this file
# to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile on your host and replace it with your own host name. Never commit
# the filled-in version anywhere.
#
# Caddy obtains and renews a Let's Encrypt certificate for this host automatically and
# redirects plain HTTP to HTTPS on its own — that is the whole reason it is here. The relay
# itself speaks plain HTTP on loopback only and never terminates TLS.
#
# The proxy target must match the relay's Kestrel endpoint. That is
# `Kestrel__Endpoints__Http__Url` in the relay's configuration, which defaults to
# http://127.0.0.1:5000 (source/FoodUsRelay/appsettings.json). Change one, change the other.

relay.example.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5000
}
